# Compiler rewrite goal

The active project goal is a **feature-complete Nucleus compiler whose core
(code + immutable) aims at 12,288 bytes**. The 16 KiB bank is the hard gate,
not the target. Read `docs/plans/2026-08-16-compiler-rewrite.md` before size
or architecture work.

Required in the destination: `string[]`, `T[]`, `i8`/`i16`, nested arrays.
Keep no-pointers, no-heap, streaming one-pass, interned types, scalar locals,
and the proof harness.

Do not weaken the language to fit. Treat parser/emit representation changes as
redesign. Rewrite in place with proofs green at every step. Re-census the
current core before acting on old site counts.
